workedExample:
Imagine you receive an API response that looks like this: `{"user":{"id":101,"name":"John Doe","roles":["admin","user"],"active":true}}`. It's hard to read at a glance. When you paste this into the JSON Formatter, it outputs:

{
  "user": {
    "id": 101,
    "name": "John Doe",
    "roles": [
      "admin",
      "user"
    ],
    "active": true
  }
}

Now the hierarchical structure is immediately obvious.
